QuestGuidance.Register("en",98,{
[3105]="7004728E\n1\tGo to Thorin's throne room in the Hall under the Mountain\tThorin III, King under the Mountain, is at his throne in Erebor.\n2\tTalk to Gimli in the throne room in the Hall under the Mountain\tGimli, son of Glóin, has come to Erebor to speak with the King under the Mountain.\n3\tTalk to King Thorin III at his throne in the Hall under the Mountain\tThorin III, King under the Mountain, is at his throne in Erebor.\n4\tDwarves of Erebor that may wish to accompany Gimli to the Glittering Caves can be found throughout the Hall under the Mountain.\t\n5\tTalk to Gimli by the provisioner in the Hall under the Mountain\tGimli is near the provisioner in the Hall under the Mountain, arranging for the things he will need on his expedition.\n",
[3106]="70047B4F\n1\tTalk to Pippin\tYou should talk to Pippin and Merry in Bâr Thorenion to learn what serious matters they have been discussing.\n2\tTalk to Merry\tYou should talk to Pippin and Merry in Bâr Thorenion to learn what serious matters they have been discussing.\n3\tReturn to Flooded Isengard\tPippin and Merry have asked you to visit Flooded Isengard and look in after Saruman, the Ents, and anything that will reveal what the three half-orcs were talking about.\n4\tFind the other Ents\tYou have found Quickbeam in the waters of Flooded Isengard, who has told you that Treebeard and several other Ents are gathered up ahead on the western side of Orthanc, discussing Saruman.\n5\tTalk to Treebeard\tYou have found Quickbeam in the waters of Flooded Isengard, who has told you that Treebeard and several other Ents are gathered on the western side of Orthanc, discussing Saruman.\n6\tExamine Barrel of Pipe-weed\tTreebeard suggested that you search for other clues around Flooded Isengard, while you wait for Saruman to emerge from Orthanc.\n7\tReturn to Treebeard\tYou discovered many more barrels of pipe-weed than Merry and Pippin had found, and packaged over the course of nearly two years, as well. You should return to Treebeard where he stands before the west face of Orthanc in Flooded Isengard.\n8\tApproach Orthanc\tYou should approach Orthanc from where the Ents stand on the western side of Flooded Isengard and see if Saruman will speak with you.\n9\tListen to Saruman\tSaruman stands high upon his tower on the western side of Flooded Isengard. Saruman has asked you to listen to his plea.\n10\tLook around you\tSaruman stands high upon his tower on the western side of Flooded Isengard. Saruman has said that if you free him, he will heal, regrow, and make reparations for the wrongs done in his name. You should look around to consider the weight of his words.\n11\tListen to Saruman\tSaruman stands high upon his tower on the western side of Flooded Isengard. You should listen once more to Saruman's plea.\n12\tConsider dethroned Mordor\tSaruman stands high upon his tower on the western side of Flooded Isengard. Saruman has suggested that he could aid in the subjugation and cleansing of Mordor, still covered in the corruptions, lieutenants, and shadow of Sauron as it is. You should consider the dethroned land and what Saruman might do there.\n13\tSaruman stands high upon his tower on the western side of Flooded Isengard. You should listen one last time to Saruman's plea.\t\n14\tConsider the Free Peoples\tSaruman stands high upon his tower on the western side of Flooded Isengard. Saruman has suggested that he could employ his vast wisdom to bring prosperity to the Free Peoples. You should consider how this possibility might turn out.\n15\tGo back to Treebeard\tTreebeard and another Ent stand before Orthanc on the western side of Flooded Isengard. You have heard Saruman's three pleas and seen through each ploy. Now you should return to Treebeard and see what he has to say.\n16\tReturn to Pippin and Merry\tYou should return to Pippin and Merry in Bâr Thorenion with word of all that you have seen and heard.\n",
[3107]="7001424D\n1\tTalk to Wárr\tWárr is in the Chamber of Mazarbul, located to the right off the north hallway that leaves the Twenty-first Hall, in Zelem-melek. Brogur has told you that Wárr has been asking for your help with something in the Chamber of Mazarbul.\n2\tDebris litters the Chamber of Mazarbul, on the right side of the north hallway leaving the Twenty-first Hall in Zelem-melek. Wárr has asked you to search the debris in the Chamber of Mazarbul for anything of interest that might be useful to the dwarves.\t\n3\tBring the Book of Mazarbul to Brogur\tBrogur is in the Chamber of Leadership off the Twenty-first Hall in Zelem-melek. You found a mysterious book in the rubble of the Chamber of Mazarbul and should show it to Brogur at once.\n4\tBring the Book of Mazarbul to Bósi\tBósi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, at the southern entrance to Durin's Way, north of the Great Delving. Brogur has been greatly upset by the tale recorded in the Book of Mazarbul, and has asked you to bring the grim tome to Bósi.\n",
[3108]="700472A0\n1\tTalk to King Elessar in his throne room\tKing Elessar is in his throne room atop Minas Tirith.\n2\tTalk to Gimli in the throne room of King Elessar\030Talk to Legolas in the throne room of King Elessar\tLegolas and Gimli have come to the throne room of King Elessar and wish to speak with you.\n3\tFind the gift of the dwarves on the south-east side of the Second Circle, in Minas Tirith\tThe gift of the dwarves Gimli brought to Minas Tirith is currently on the south-east side of the Second Circle.\n4\tFind the gift of the Elves on the south-east side of the Second Circle, in Minas Tirith\tThe gift of the Elves Legolas brought to Minas Tirith is currently on the south-east side of the Second Circle.\n5\tTalk to Dúnor on the south-east side of the Second Circle, in Minas Tirith\tDúnor is on the south-east side of the Second Circle in Minas Tirith, and is having trouble dealing with an unruly crowd.\n6\tSpeak to members of the unruly crowd and try to calm them down\tDúnor has asked for your help in calming the unruly crowd on the south-east side of the Second Circle, in Minas Tirith.\n7\tSpeak to members of the unruly crowd and try to calm them down\tDúnor has asked for your help in calming the unruly crowd on the south-east side of the Second Circle, in Minas Tirith.\n8\tSpeak to members of the unruly crowd and try to calm them down\tDúnor has asked for your help in calming the unruly crowd on the south-east side of the Second Circle, in Minas Tirith.\n9\tTalk to Dúnor on the south-east side of the Second Circle, in Minas Tirith\tDúnor is on the south-east side of the Second Circle, in Minas Tirith.\n10\tTalk to King Elessar in his throne room\tKing Elessar is in his throne room atop Minas Tirith.\n",
[3109]="70014669\n1\tTalk to Bori and assault Zabadgathol\tBori is in the Chamber of Leadership off the Twenty-first Hall, in Zelem-melek. Bori has decided upon a new plan: to attack Mazog's fortress, wielding Zigilburk, and to slay the evil Orc before the force out of Dol Guldur can take advantage of the situation between the Orcs and the dwarves.\n2\tTalk to Brogur\tBrogur is in the Deep-way. After Bori's failed assault on Zabadgathol, Brogur has moved to the Deep-way where he mourns the loss of both his nephew and Zigilburk.\n",
[3110]="7001A97A\n1\tTalk to Alfirimbes and travel with the Hidden Guard\tAlfirimbes is at the Elf-camp of Echad Sirion in the Mirk-eaves. The Hidden Guard is ready to begin the first leg of the journey to bring Mazog to Dol Guldur, by way of the Drownholt. Alfirimbes will bring you to them.\n2\tTalk to Cúcheron on the front porch of the Haunted Inn\tCúcheron is on the front porch of the Haunted Inn, mourning the loss of Raddir. Raddir may be gone, but the mission of the Hidden Guard must continue. Cúcheron will tell you what should be done as the Elves try to regroup from the loss of one of their own.\n",
[3111]="70025372\n1\tTalk to Nona in Lhanuch\tNona is in the north-eastern corner of Lhanuch. Candaith has asked you to check on Nona to see how she is dealing with the death of her brother.\n2\tRecover the sword from Wadu's favourite tree\tWadu's favourite tree is on a rise west of Lhanuch, overlooking the ox-pens. Nona has asked you to recover the Rohirrim sword she left at Wadu's favourite tree. It was found with Wadu's body and she thought to leave it there as a remembrance, but has changed her mind.\n3\tBring Wadu's sword to Nona in the north-east corner of Lhanuch\tNona is in the north-eastern corner of Lhanuch. You have recovered the sword from Wadu's favourite tree and should now bring it to Nona as she requested.\n4\tTalk to Halbarad in Lhanuch\tHalbarad is in Lhanuch, among the huts on the western side of the village. Nona has asked to accompany the Grey Company when it departs Lhanuch and travels south.\n",
[3112]="700145BA\n1\tAid Rink Stronghammer with his preparations\tRink Stronghammer is in the Heart of Fire, off the Way of Smiths, among the Silvertine Lodes. Stóthkell has asked you to aid his lieutenant with preparations for the defence of the Heart of Fire.\n2\tTalk to Stóthkell in the Heart of Fire, off the Way of Smiths\tStóthkell is in the Heart of Fire, off the Way of Smiths, among the Silvertine Lodes. You have aided Rink Stronghammer with his preparations and should now report of your successes to Stóthkell.\n",
[3113]="700145BC\n1\tDefeat goblin-runners in the Water-works (total: 5)\tGoblin-runners bring word of the enemy's plans throughout the Water-works. Rink Stronghammer wants you to defeat goblin runners, thus disrupting goblin communications in the Water-works.\n2\tTalk to Rink Stronghammer\tRink Stronghammer is in the Heart of Fire, off the Way of Smiths among the Silvertine Lodes. You have disrupted goblin communications in the Water-works and should now return to Rink Stronghammer.\n",
[3114]="70014750\n1\tTalk to Orophin\030Talk to Rúmil\tRúmil and Orophin are stationed along the boundaries of Lothlórien. Haldir told you to walk along the north bank of the river Nimrodel to find his brothers. Haldir has asked you to lend your aid to Rúmil and Orophin. They do not speak much of the Common Tongue, so if you cannot speak to them in Elvish, your mutual hatred of the Orcs must transcend the need for words.\n2\tTalk to Haldir\tHaldir is at his camp on the boundary of Lothlórien. You have spoken with his brothers and repelled an attack by the Orcs, and should return now to Haldir.\n",
[3115]="7002093E\n1\tTalk to Saeradan in Bree-land\tSaeradan is at his cabin in Bree-land, east of Thornley's Worksite in the Northern Bree-fields. Candaith has told you to travel next to tell Ranger Saeradan of the Grey Company's road.\n2\tTalk to Barliman Butterbur at The Prancing Pony Inn\tBarliman Butterbur is the proprietor of The Prancing Pony and can be found by its bar, in the town of Bree. Saeradan has agreed to travel south with the Grey Company, but he wants you to ask Barliman Butterbur to be careful while the Rangers are gone.\n3\tRetrieve foodstuffs from a crate in the Pony\tCrates of foodstuffs are waiting in one of the parlours of The Prancing Pony. Barliman has heard the warning you brought from Saeradan, but he seems to have already forgotten it, and has asked you to carry foodstuffs out to the main room of the Pony.\n4\tRetrieve foodstuffs from a crate in the Pony\tCrates of foodstuffs are waiting in one of the parlours of The Prancing Pony. Barliman has heard the warning you brought from Saeradan, but he seems to have already forgotten it, and has asked you to carry foodstuffs out to the main room of the Pony.\n5\tRetrieve foodstuffs from a crate in the Pony\tCrates of foodstuffs are waiting in one of the parlours of The Prancing Pony. Barliman has heard the warning you brought from Saeradan, but he seems to have already forgotten it, and has asked you to carry foodstuffs out to the main room of the Pony.\n6\tTalk to Barliman Buttebur at The Prancing Pony Inn\tBarliman Butterbur is in the main room of The Prancing Pony. You have carried several loads of foodstuffs from one of the Pony's parlours out to the main room and should speak now to Barliman.\n7\tTalk to Uchdrud at The Prancing Pony Inn\tUchdrud is sitting at a table in the main room of The Prancing Pony. Barliman Butterbur has asked you to encourage Uchdrud, an unruly and coarse sort, to vacate the premises.\n8\tMeet Uchdrud outside the North-gate of Bree\tUchdrud is waiting somewhere by the North-gate of Bree for you to answer his challenge. You did as Butterbur asked and told Uchdrud to finish his beer and leave the Pony, and he reacted angrily, challenging you to meet him outside the North Gate of Bree.\n9\tTalk to Saeradan at his cabin\tSaeradan is at his cabin outside the town of Bree. You have done as Saeradan asked and should now return to him at his cabin.\n",
[3116]="700145BB\n1\tSearch piles of old weapons for useable materials (total: 8)\tWafi gave you a list of places to search for debris piles that might contain useable weapons that can be melted down by the craftsmen at the Heart of Fire. Wafi needs raw materials with which to craft equipment for the defence of the Heart of Fire and has asked you to search debris piles throughout Moria for useable weapons.\n2\tBring suitable weapons and the list to Wafi\tWafi is in the Heart of Fire, off the Way of Smiths among the Silvertine Lodes. You have collected many suitable weapons that can be melted down for use in the forges of the Heart of Fire.\n",
[3117]="70018F0B\n1\tTalk to Legolas\tLegolas is standing next to Gimli atop the flet above the hill of Cerin Amroth. You have been invited by Gimli to patrol the woods of Lothlórien with Legolas and himself, and should speak now with the Elf about the excursion.\n2\tTalk to Legolas and travel with him through the Golden Wood\tLegolas is standing next to Gimli atop the flet above the hill of Cerin Amroth. You have been invited by Gimli to patrol the woods of Lothlórien with him and Legolas, and should speak to Legolas when you are ready to go.\n3\tTalk to Gimli\tGimli is on a flet among the trees above the hill of Cerin Amroth, in the centre of Lórien. Celeborn has agreed to help the Iron Garrison overcome its problems within Moria, and you should speak to Gimli about what has happened.\n",
[3118]="7005A6AA\n1\tCollect ingots near the upper forges (total: 12)\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. You should collect some ingots at the upper forges in Vérnozal.\n2\tForge Zhélruka weapons (quantity: see journal)\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. You should forge some Zhélruka weapons in Vérnozal.\n3\tTalk to Prince Ingór\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. Prince Ingór wishes to talk to you.\n4\tTalk to Prince Ingór\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. Prince Ingór wishes to talk to you.\n5\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. You should give the Zhélruka weapons to the visiting Longbeard captains.\t\n6\tTalk to Prince Ingór\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. Prince Ingór wishes to talk to you.\n",
[3119]="7002161B\n1\tTalk to Candaith in Rivendell and experience 'Session: The House of Isildur' or read the shortened account instead\tCandaith is at the stables of Rivendell. Candaith has offered to tell you of key moments in the history of the Dúnedain.\n2\tTalk to Candaith in Rivendell\tCandaith is by the stables in Rivendell. You have listened to Candaith describe some of the history of the Dúnedain and should speak to him now for the conclusion.\n",
[3120]="70013AF5\n1\tBring the dusty pages to Bori\tBori is in a small room off the eastern side of the Chamber of the Cross-roads. Bósi has given you back the dusty pages which hold clues to the location of Zigilburk, hoping that your delivery may raise his son's spirits.\n2\tFind evidence of Katûb-zahar\tKatûb-zahar, the Word-hoard of Durin, is somewhere on the eastern side of the Great Delving, north of a large statue of Durin. Bori told you that if you can find the place called Katûb-zahar, he may be able to discover the location of the mysterious mithril axe, Zigilburk.\n3\tTalk to Bori\tBori is in the Chamber of Command; it is the room up the eastern stairs in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, at the southern end of Durin's Way. It can be reached from the Great Delving. You have located a plaque that marks the location of Katûb-zahar and should return to Bori with the news.\n",
[3121]="70065B5E\n1\tTalk to King Elessar outside the keep of Lond Cirion\tKing Elessar is outside the keep of Lond Cirion.\n2\tDefeat beasts or spirits in Thingast (total: 6)\tThingast has a reputation for being haunted, and the folk of Lond Cirion will appreciate if you face some of the dangers there as you journey north.\n3\tTravel to the entrance of Iáphel in Tûm Rost\tIáphel is located north of Thingast, in Tûm Rost.\n4\tTalk to Grethril by the entrance to Iáphel\tGrethril is at the entrance of Iáphel in Tûm Rost.\n5\tTalk to Gwindir north-west of the entrance of Iáphel\tGwindir is north-west of the entrance to Iáphel.\n6\tPick grapes from the vines at Iáphel (total: 6)\tVine trellises can be found on the western side of Iáphel.\n7\tBring the grapes to Gwindir in Iáphel\tGwindir is waiting for you to return with the grapes you picked.\n8\tSelect wines for the King's company (total: 3)\tGwindir offered you three of the wines stored nearby.\n9\tBring the wine bottles to Grethril by the entrance to Iáphel\tGrethril will know how best to store the wine bottles. She is by the entrance to Iáphel.\n10\tTalk to King Elessar at Iáphel\tKing Elessar is in Iáphel.\n",
[3122]="700583F8\n1\tTalk to Thálfi beside the river just north-west of Annâk-khurfu\tThálfi is beside the river just north-west of Annâk-khurfu, preparing to scout the mountainous region in advance of the assault.\n2\tUse the map-ready parchment to add Zarkul-sulûn to the map\030Use the map-ready parchment to add Shakal-atrâd to the map\030Use the map-ready parchment to add Howlers' Notch to the map\tThálfi sent you to add three locations to the parchment he gave you: two old dwarf ruins to the north-west and south-west, and a warg camp further north-west.\n3\tTalk to Thálfi at Zudramdân, north-east of the lake that borders the foothills\tThálfi is at Zudramdân, the forward camp of Durin's great force. Zudramdân is north-east of the lake that borders the foothills of Elderslade.\n4\tUse the map-ready parchment to add Caivád Sâr to the map\030Defeat Angmarim in Elderslade (total: 6)\tThálfi wanted you to add the Angmarim presence at Caivád Sâr to your map, and to defeat any of the cultists that cross your path. Caivád Sâr is to the north of Zudramdân.\n5\tBring the map back to Thálfi at Zudramdân\tThálfi is at Zudramdân, the forward camp of Durin's great force, south of Caivád Sâr.\n",
[3123]="70048C5F\n1\tIntercept a message near the Spire of Lûghash\030Intercept a message near Fushaum Bal\030Intercept a message from Orodir, the camp outside Naerband\030Intercept a message near the Tower of Cirith Ungol\030All intercepted messages can be read from your inventory\tOrcs and evil Men of every variety near the Spire of Lûghash, the settlement of Fushaum Bal, the tower of Cirith Ungol, and the camp outside Naerband may carry messages from their masters to Lhaereth the Stained.\n2\tBring the intercepted messages to Harthalín by the eastward road in Agarnaith\030All intercepted messages can be read from your inventory\tHarthalín is by the eastward-running road in Agarnaith.\n",
[3124]="70065B5F\n1\tTravel to the northern entrance of the keep of Ost Arndír, north-east of Iáphel\tThe entrance to Ost Arndír is to the north-east of Iáphel, in Pinnath Gelin.\n2\tTalk to Hebron outside the keep of Ost Arndír\tHebron is outside the northern entrance to the keep of Ost Arndír.\n3\tTalk to Lady Nauriel in Ost Arndír\tThe Lady Nauriel is inside the main hall of Ost Arndír, located upstairs inside the keep.\n4\tFind Thorongil's room inside the keep of Ost Arndír\tNauriel's son Thorongil's room is to the north-east, through the door on the right.\n5\tTalk to Thorongil inside his room in the keep of Ost Arndír\tThorongil is in his room north of the main hall, inside the keep of Ost Arndír.\n6\tTalk to Orgolas in Thorongil's room inside the keep of Ost Arndír\tOrgolas is in Thorongil's room in Ost Arndír.\n7\tTalk to Hebron in Ost Arndír\tHebron is outside the northern entrance of the keep of Ost Arndír.\n8\tDefeat foes throughout Pinnath Gelin (total: 10)\tAccording to Hebron, various dangers can be found in the vicinity of Ost Arndír, and the folk of the town would appreciate you helping deal with them.\n9\tTalk to Hebron outside the northern entrance of the keep in Ost Arndír\tHebron is outside the northern entrance of the keep in Ost Arndír.\n10\tTalk to Thorongil outside the keep of Ost Arndír\tThorongil is outside the northern entrance of the keep of Ost Arndír.\n",
[3125]="7005840F\n1\tScout the bridge in front of Gundabad\030Scout the central courtyard in front of Gundabad\030Scout the settlement of Dûn Traikh beyond the entrance to Gundabad\030Defeat Orc-kind in Elderslade (total: 10)\030Defeat Angmarim in Elderslade (total: 10)\tThálfi wants you to scout enemy camps nearer to Gundabad and to defeat any Orcs and Angmarim you find on the way. This time he has not asked you to draw the locations on a map, and will rely instead upon your report. Crossing the bridge in front of Gundabad and exploring past the central courtyard on your way to the buildings beyond the entrance should be sufficient.\n2\tTalk to Thálfi at Zudramdân in Elderslade\tThálfi is at Zudramdân in Elderslade.\n3\tTalk to Imák at Zudramdân in Elderslade\tImák is at Zudramdân in Elderslade, and he wishes to speak with you.\n",
[3126]="70048C60\n1\tTalk to Zaghárog outside the Caverns of Fire, in Talath Úrui\tThe watching-stone inhabited by the spirit Zaghárog is on the road to the Caverns of Fire, in Talath Úrui.\n2\tZaghárog showed you a particular area in Lhingris and asked you to kill the creature there.\t\n3\tTalk to Zaghárog outside the Caverns of Fire, in Talath Úrui\tThe watching-stone inhabited by the spirit Zaghárog is on the road to the Caverns of Fire, in Talath Úrui.\n4\tZaghárog told you to walk to the north-west\tZaghárog told you to walk to the north-west. Will this provide your answer?\n5\tTalk to Harthalín by the road to Nargroth\tHarthalín is by the road to Nargroth, on the eastern edge of Talath Úrui.\n",
[3127]="70065B6C\n1\tTalk to Orgolas outside the keep of Ost Arndír\tOrgolas is outside the keep of Ost Arndír.\n2\tThere is no stopping them\tThe boys have run off on their adventure.\n3\tFind Daeram at the keep's kitchens in Ost Arndír and tell him where the boys planned to go\tDaeram is inside the kitchens of the keep in Ost Arndír.\n4\tFind Orgolas and Thorongil near the Wave-hunter\tOrgolas and Thorongil intended to go to the Wave-hunter, docked to the east on the lake in Pinnath Gelin.\n5\tTalk to Orgolas near the Wave-hunter\tOrgolas is near the Wave-hunter, peering up at the rigging.\n6\tTalk to Daeram near the Wave-hunter\tDaeram is near the Wave-hunter.\n7\tCross onto the deck of the Wave-hunter\tYou should cross onto the deck of the Wave-hunter in order to get Thorongil to come down.\n8\tFrom the deck of the Wave-hunter, beckon for Thorongil to come down\tFrom the deck of the Wave-hunter you should beckon for Thorongil to come down.\n9\tWait for Thorongil to come down\tThorongil is high above your head in the rigging of the Wave-hunter.\n10\tTalk to Thorongil on the deck of the Wave-hunter\tThorongil stands on the deck of the Wave-hunter.\n11\tTalk to Orgolas near the Wave-hunter\tOrgolas stands near the Wave-hunter.\n12\tReturn to the northern entrance of the keep of Ost Arndír, west of the Wave-hunter\tThe northern entrance to the keep of Ost Arndír is west of the Wave-hunter.\n13\tTalk to Hebron outside the keep of Ost Arndír\tHebron is outside the keep of Ost Arndír.\n",
[3128]="70048C65\n1\tTalk to Mithrandir in the First Circle of Minas Tirith, south of the entrance to the city\tMithrandir is in the First Circle of Minas Tirith, south of the entrance to the city.\n2\tFind the group of freed Nurnhoth on the north-east side of the Third Circle\tA group of freed Nurnhoth might be found on the north-east side of the Third Circle, in Minas Tirith.\n3\tTalk to Hujâ on the north-east side of the Third Circle, in Minas Tirith\tHujâ is among a group of freed Nurnhoth on the north-east side of the Third Circle, in Minas Tirith.\n4\tBring the Nurnhoth clothes to Lain, a tailor on the south-eastern side of the Third Circle\tThe tailor on the south-eastern side of the Third Circle will be able to fashion a disguise of the appropriate size from the Nurnhoth clothes that were given to you by Hujâ.\n5\tTalk to Ayorzén on the south-eastern side of the Third Circle\tAyorzén has followed you to the tailor, and is now on the south-eastern side of the Third Circle, seeking to get your attention.\n6\tTalk to Mithrandir at Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate\tMithrandir is in Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate.\n",
[3129]="70058410\n1\tCollect sapper-bombs from goblins in Elderslade (total: 5)\030Collect loose rocks from the base of cliffs in Elderslade (total: 8)\tGoblins carry sapper-bombs that Imák wants for his plan. He also wants you to collect some loose, heavy rocks from the base of cliffs north of Zudramdân in Elderslade.\n2\tBring the goblin-bombs and loose rocks to Imák at Zudramdân\tImák is at Zudramdân in Elderslade. You have collected a number of sapper-bombs and loose rocks and should bring them back to Imák.\n3\tTalk to Thálfi at Zudramdân\tThálfi is at Zudramdân in Elderslade.\n4\tTalk to Durin on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu\tDurin is on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu.\n5\tTalk to Prince Ingór on the lower level of Annâk-khurfu\tPrince Ingór is on the lower level of Annâk-khurfu.\n6\tTalk to Durin on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu\tDurin is on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu.\n",
[3130]="70065B6D\n1\tTalk to Nauriel in Ost Arndír\tNauriel is inside the main hall of the keep in Ost Arndír.\n2\tTalk to King Elessar in the main hall of the keep of Ost Arndír\tKing Elessar is inside the main hall of the keep in Ost Arndír.\n3\tTalk to King Elessar in the keep of Ost Arndír and join the defence of Tûm Rost\tKing Elessar hopes to bring his own fighters to join the defence of Tûm Rost against the Corsair raiders.\n4\tTalk to Nauriel in the main hall of the keep of Ost Arndír\tNauriel is inside the main hall of the keep in Ost Arndír.\n5\tTalk to King Elessar in Ost Arndír\tKing Elessar is inside the main hall of the keep of Ost Arndír.\n",
[3131]="70058428\n1\tTalk to Durin and begin the assault upon Gundabad\tDurin is on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu, waiting to give the word for the assault to begin.\n2\tTalk to Durin inside Zarkul-sulûn during the War of Three Peaks\tDurin is inside Zarkul-sulûn, commanding his forces amid the chaos of the War of Three Peaks.\n3\tTalk to Prince Ingór north-east of Zarkul-sulûn during the War of Three Peaks\tPrince Ingór is north-east of Zarkul-sulûn during the War of Three Peaks, standing atop a barricade and commanding his Zhélruka.\n",
[3132]="70048C66\n1\tTalk to Mithrandir and travel to the meeting of the Masters of Mordor\tMithrandir is at Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate.\n2\tTalk to Mithrandir at Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate\tMithrandir is at Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate.\n",
[3133]="70058429\n1\tCollect fallen Zhélruka weapons (total: 6)\030Defeat enemy forces during the War of Three Peaks (total: 12)\tPrince Ingór wants you to pick up weapons dropped by his slain warriors as proof that the Zhélruka are shouldering their own share of the war's burden. You should also slay any enemies that break through the line.\n2\tBring the Zhélruka weapons to the weapon crate in the trench to the north-west\tA crate for storing spare weapons can be found in a trench north-west of Prince Ingór's defensive position during the War of Three Peaks.\n3\tTalk to Bori in the trench north-west of Zarkul-sulûn during the War of Three Peaks\tBori is in the trench north-west of Zarkul-sulûn during the War of Three Peaks.\n4\tFind Bróin or Bósi north-west of Bori's trench\tBori wanted you to look for his cousin Bróin or his father Bósi north-west of his trench. He has not seen them since the fighting began, and he is worried for their safety.\n5\tFind the retreating dwarves Bósi saw near the trench to the north\tBósi told you he saw dwarves retreating from thick fighting to the north. You should search there for Bróin.\n6\tTalk to Trausti in the trench not far from the lakeside during the War of Three Peaks\tYou found Trausti in a trench not far from the lakeside while the fighting rages all about him and the War of Three Peaks continues.\n",
[3134]="70065CFC\n1\tTravel to the southern coast of Thingast, south-west of Lond Cirion, in Anfalas\tKing Elessar wants you to travel with haste to the coast near Thingast, south-west of Lond Cirion, in Anfalas.\n2\tLook out over the water for the fleeing Corsair ships from the coast of Thingast\tFrom this location on the coast you should look out over the water in search of the fleeing Corsair ships.\n3\tLook out over the water for the fleeing Corsair ships\030Find a spot further to the west from which you might spy distant ships\tAnother location on the coast to the west may allow you to look out over the water in search of the fleeing Corsair ships.\n4\tTalk to Arasdil on the coast of Thingast\tArasdil stands nearby, and has something to say to you.\n5\tSearch the grove to the south-west for sign of the Corsairs\tArasdil told you he saw Corsair activity at the haunted grove to the south-west before the ships sailed toward Pinnath Gelin.\n6\tExamine the high-quality bow on the stone block\tA high quality bow rests on a stone within the grove here.\n7\tRemain on your guard\tYou feel the sudden sensation of being watched.\n8\tTalk to the Ent in the shady grove\tA mighty Ent stares at you from within the curious, deep wells of his eyes.\n",
[3135]="7005842B\n1\tFind Bróin somewhere to the north, where Trausti last saw him\tTrausti last saw Bróin and Slagvi fighting side-by-side to the north, while battle raged on all around them.\n2\tTalk to Bróin as he works to free Slagvi from the rock trap\tSlagvi has been trapped by a fall of stones, and Bróin is trying to free him from the heavy rocks.\n3\tUse Rock-pile\tSlagvi has been trapped by a fall of stones, and Bróin is trying to free him from the heavy rocks. Bróin wants you to help him free Slagvi from the rocks, and he will need you to defend them while he works!\n4\tBróin helps Slagvi to safety!\t\n5\tMeet up with Slagvi several trenches to the south during the War of Three Peaks\tMeet up with Slagvi in a trench to the south while the War of Three Peaks continues.\n6\tFind Imák outside Zarkul-sulûn during the War of Three Peaks\tSlagvi cannot believe his ears: the trap in which he was caught had been set by the Stout-axe Imák? He demands that you find Imák and ask why he has chosen to fight dwarves and not Orcs.\n7\tTalk to Imák outside Zarkul-sulûn during the War of Three Peaks\tImák is outside Zarkul-sulûn during the War of Three Peaks, surrounded by an angry group of Longbeards.\n8\tCollect and defuse the goblin-bombs from the crate where Imák stored them, inside Zarkul-sulûn\tImák has reluctantly agreed not to use the goblin-bombs you collected. He sent you to collect the bombs from the crate where he stored them, inside Zarkul-sulûn, and render them unusable.\n9\tTalk to Afwald by the empty crate in Zarkul-sulûn, during the War of Three Peaks\tThe dwarf Afwald stands near the empty crate where Imák stored the goblin-bombs, in Zarkul-sulûn. You should ask him what happened to the explosive devices.\n",
[3136]="70065D0A\n1\tTalk to Leafshade at Tumbamálë\tThe Ent Leafshade is at the grove of Tumbamálë.\n2\tTalk to Leafshade at Tumbamálë and learn what you can from the Ent\tThe Ent Leafshade is at the grove of Tumbamálë.\n3\tTalk to Leafshade at Tumbamálë\tThe Ent Leafshade is at Tumbamálë, and he has much to say.\n4\tTalk to King Elessar inside the main hall of the keep of Lond Cirion\tKing Elessar is inside the main hall of the keep of Lond Cirion, and should hear what you learned from Leafshade.\n",
})
